{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793885823,"nonce":"LxXTeENZvN4KRs5e+gPjqufHqPA=","title":"Expose IconSet signatures without compiling SVGs during editor analysis","message":"The published Remix catalogue makes the language server execute the full SVG parser and path compiler for every icon even though editor analysis needs the public names, docs, and SvgDocument types. In the local real-LSP probe this work takes minutes and exceeds the normal five-second macro allowance.\n\nUse the standard display define to generate the complete public constant catalogue and preserve name-collision checks and module dependencies, without generating runtime SVG documents, caches, or getter bodies. Normal builds must continue validating and compiling every SVG. Rayzor also needs to expose display consistently during editor typing and syntax checks; its related tracker is 057f6096e757cdd9c7f0615e528bd8e54761d98f68a02f9ae45ce166158e93d6.\n\nThe display fixture compiles under Haxe, including a malformed runtime SVG whose constant remains typed for editor use. The existing normal IconSets program builds and runs under installed Ash with all 12 geometry, lazy allocation, cache, tint, and layout checks passing. End-to-end default-budget LSP checks and package publication remain pending.","files":null}]}